    "title": "Are malls open on Easter Sunday in South Florida? Here’s a rundown - AOL",
    "text": "Howard CohenApr 3, 20260Is your favorite South Florida mall open on Easter Sunday?It depends on your favorite.Some of the major malls in Miami-Dade and Broward are running on the holiday — and others aren’t.Here’s a look at what South Florida malls are open and closed on Easter Sunday, April 5:Shopping mallsAventura Mall in 2025. (Courtesy Aventura)Here are the malls that are open or closed on Easter:AventuraMall: Open 11 a.m.-8 p.m.Bayside Marketplace: Open 11 a.m.-9 p.m.Brickell City Centre: Shops are closed, but the CMX movie theater and restaurants are open.Broward Mall: Closed.Coral Square Mall: Closed.Dadeland Mall: Closed.DolphinMall: Open 11 a.m.-8 p.m.The Falls: Closed.Miami InternationalMall: Closed.Palms at Town & Country: Open.Sawgrass Mills: Open 11 a.m.-8 p.m.SouthlandMall: Closed.WestlandMall: Closed.In this file photo from Easter Sunday, April 17, 2022, children and families celebrated Miami Gardens’ Easter Day Eggstravaganza that featured a helicopter egg drop, live performances, food trucks, a Kid Zone, rides, games, and other family oriented entertainment. (Carl Juste/cjuste@miamiherald.com)Show comments0From Our PartnersDon't miss our daily roundup.Stay informed with a handpicked selection of the day's top AOL stories, delivered to your inbox.*Invalid email addressThanks for signing up.Thank you for signing up. You will receive a confirmation email shortly.Stay informed with a handpicked selection of the day's top AOL stories, delivered to your inbox.*Invalid email addressIn Other NewsEntertainmentEntertainmentEntertainment Weekly'Hunger Games' actor arrested on 3 counts of assault with a deadly weapon with intent…FinanceFinanceCNNChina says its economy is accelerating despite Iran war turmoil — for nowFinanceAssociated PressCould more cattle cause record beef prices to drop? Ranchers say it's not that simpleFoodFoodAllrecipesI asked 3 chefs for their favorite fast food fried chicken sandwich, and it's not Chi…FoodPeopleNutella announces first new flavor in over 60 years. Find out what it is!Lighter SideLighter SideThe Today ShowJill Scott's family photos were found at a Goodwill, then returned thanks to a viral …Lighter SideReutersIn tough times, Russians are turning to magicSportsSportsField Level MediaTyrese Maxey (31 points) sends 76ers past Magic, into playoffsSportsAssociated PressLikelihood of NFL replacement refs enters new stage with background checks, physicalsWeatherWeatherAssociated PressFloodwaters inundate Wisconsin streets, trapping drivers, as Midwest rebuilds after s…WeatherAssociated PressParts of Northern Marianas could be without power for weeks after super typhoonAdvertisementAnimals|Business|Celebrity|Entertainment|Finance|Food|Health|News|Politics|Shopping|Sports|Style|True CrimeFeedbackHelpJoin AOLAccessibilityEU Digital Services ActTerms and Privacy PolicyPrivacy DashboardAbout UsAbout our AdsAdvertisingLicensingSitemap© 2026 AOL Media LLC. All rights reserved.",
